WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.553
The “Website inbox”

2
00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:05.616
brings shares, appointment requests and messages from avrastro.com.

3
00:00:06.081 --> 00:00:08.959
Nothing enters your CRM until you accept it.

4
00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:12.763
For a request you press “Confirm appointment”

5
00:00:12.892 --> 00:00:14.574
or “Decline request”;

6
00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.327
when you decline, the client gets an e-mail that

7
00:00:17.327 --> 00:00:20.066
the time is not available and can choose another.

8
00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:23.352
You link it to an existing client or a new prospect,

9
00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:25.116
so it goes into your agenda.

10
00:00:26.216 --> 00:00:28.631
A call-back request becomes a call task,

11
00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:31.602
in the morning, midday or afternoon the client chose.

12
00:00:31.905 --> 00:00:36.618
And if the client changes or cancels an appointment on avrastro.com,

13
00:00:36.804 --> 00:00:39.880
you see it here and cancel it in the agenda.

14
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.118
In the “Agenda”

15
00:00:42.118 --> 00:00:45.020
you move from day to day, add a “New appointment”

16
00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.944
or a “New follow-up”, and see what is overdue and what has no date.

17
00:00:49.188 --> 00:00:50.047
The “Daily sheet”

18
00:00:50.047 --> 00:00:52.381
prints two A4 pages with the day’s

19
00:00:52.381 --> 00:00:54.970
appointments, calls and follow-ups.

20
00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.444
The days and hours you take appointments are set in the Advisor Hub on avrastro.com,

21
00:01:01.631 --> 00:01:04.092
under “Availability and profile”.

22
00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:08.434
So citizens only choose times that are genuinely free.

23
00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.694
In the next lesson:

24
00:01:10.718 --> 00:01:11.774
renewals.
